en(fish_kps) >= 2:\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(fish_kps[0] - fish_kps[1])\n                print(f'Body length in pixels: {dist:.1f}')","key":"VDyTdsJbub"},{"type":"outputs","id":"g12vKzoQ4ftXs_CJ2ee3R","children":[],"key":"l14bkDROgO"}],"key":"OsHid25hWi"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","data":{"id":"a91beea8"},"children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reflecting on Results","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"UOIYjfvn7Y"}],"identifier":"reflecting-on-results","label":"Reflecting on Results","html_id":"reflecting-on-results","implicit":true,"key":"Sa2S6PUSAP"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work through these questions after you have run inference and looked at the annotated output images saved under ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"mRJsFbxwfs"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/content/runs/pose/predict/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"oooEcuSDP5"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"rLxUD2A0hx"}],"key":"Y8wvuC3jjr"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Calibration to real-world length.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"ZWqowgwazY"}],"key":"AV09ReuAyU"},{"type":"text","value":"\nThe model outputs pixel distances, but fishery science requires measurements in centimeters or millimeters. Describe a practical calibration method you could use with the camera system available to you. What information do you need to collect in the field, and how would you propagate measurement uncertainty through the calibration step to report a final length estimate with a confidence interval?","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"xivsgUwG5S"}],"key":"FWWC3UHJW2"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Additional keypoints for richer morphometrics.","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"key":"zKTRYMnyZj"}],"key":"G7o7fJidTJ"},{"type":"text","value":"\nSnout-to-tail distance approximates standard length, but fish biologists often record several other measurements: fork length, body depth at the pectoral fin insertion, head length, and eye diameter. Which additional keypoints would you add to the label schema to capture these measurements? Consider the trade-off between annotation cost (more keypoints per image means more labeling time) and the scientific value of each additional measurement.","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"key":"btovMWiah3"}],"key":"dBiY2CATnJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Occlusion and visibility scores.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"Hk2s7EweYs"}],"key":"z7sCfjRfBV"},{"type":"text","value":"\nBlack cod in survey footage frequently swim in loose aggregations, and fins from one individual can overlap the body of another. When a keypoint is occluded, the model may still predict a location for it, but with lower confidence. How would you use the per-keypoint confidence scores returned by ","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"YdIED9XZ8w"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".conf","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"qHm7pq6cRI"},{"type":"text","value":" to filter out unreliable measurements? At what confidence threshold would you discard a length estimate, and how would you determine that threshold empirically using your validation set?","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"HfFVCLGAhx"}],"key":"TGHNsGCZF2"}],"key":"BBn1LE54TR"}],"key":"gp8EVL89XJ"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"3.8 Localizing the OceanCV FirstPass Model to a New Dataset","url":"/book/oceancvlocalizing-yolo","group":"Chapter 3 - Computer Vision Development"},"next":{"title":"3.10 Instance Segmentation with YOLO","url":"/book/instancesegmentation-yolo","group":"Chapter 3 - Computer Vision Development"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}